    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4645" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Autŏnŏē</span></b> ,
		ēs. f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αὐτονόη</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Daughter of Cadmus</i>, <i>wife of
				Aristœus</i>, <i>and mother of
				Actœon</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 3, 720</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Ib.
			469</span></i>.— Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Autŏnŏēĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			cr <i>pertaining to Autonoë</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">heros = Actaeon,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					3, 198</span></i>
			. </div>
